      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that seven identical bowling balls weigh the same as three identical canoes, we want to solve for the weight of one bowling ball or the weight of one canoe. According to the problem statement, two of the canoes weigh a combined 56 pounds. With this information, we can calculate the weight of one canoe as follows:\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total weight of two canoes.\n2 Canoes weigh 56 pounds\nEach canoe weighs: 56 / 2 = 28 pounds\n\nStep 2: Calculate the weight of three canoes.\nThree canoes weigh 3 * 28 = 84 pounds\n\nStep 3: Calculate the number of bowling balls that make up the 84 pound weight.\n3 Canoes weigh 84 pounds\nEach bowling ball weights 84 / 7 = 12 pounds\n\nGiven that the weight of one canoe combined with two of the canoes is 56 pounds and there are three canoes that weigh 84 pounds, we are also told there are seven identical bowling balls.\n\nAnswer: One bowling ball weighs 12 pounds.",
