      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let $b$ be the weight of one bowling ball and $c$ be the weight of one canoe. We can set up the following system of equations based on the given information:\n\n\\[\\begin{align*}\n7b &= 3c \\\\\n2c &= 56 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\\]\n\nWe can solve the second equation for $c$:\n\n\\[\\begin{align*}\n2c &= 56 \\\\\nc &= 28 \\end{align*}\\]\n\nSubstituting the value of $c$ into the first equation, we get:\n\n\\[\\begin{align*}\n7b &= 3(28) \\\\\n7b &= 84 \\\\\nb &= 12\n\\end{align*}\\]\n\nTherefore, one bowling ball weighs $\\boxed{12}$ pounds.",
