      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can set up and solve a simple equation.\n\nLet \"1\" = the weight of one canoe.\n\nAccording to the problem, the total weight of three canoes at left side is 3 * 1.\n\nThe 7 identical bowling balls weigh the same as 3 canoes at right side, then 7 * x.\n\nWe can accordingly set up the equation:\n\n3 * 1 = 7 * x\n\nSimplify and solve to get the answer:\n\n1) Divide both sides of the equation by 3\n\n1 = 7 * x / 3\n4.5 = 7x\n\n2) Divide both sides of the equation by 7\n\n4.5/7 = x\n0.642857 = x\n\nTherefore, one of the bowling balls weighs x = 0.642857 pounds.",
